// `desk-keeps-five.rho` with ONE token changed: the guard now names Church 6. Same three terms,
// same channel, same receive pattern, same order in the file — a different answer comes out.
//
// So the guard is genuinely DECIDED, not failing closed: a guard the substrate could not decide
// would reject everything and this file would publish nothing. And Church 5 was resting on
// @"results" during the previous run all along — the desk SELECTS out of the set, it does not
// consume it.
//
// EXPECT   @"OUT" = Church numeral 6      (5 and 0 left resting on @"results")

@"results"!(lambda:Term`lam f. lam x. (f, (f, (f, (f, (f, x)))))`) |
@"results"!(lambda:Term`lam f. lam x. (f, (f, (f, (f, (f, (f, x))))))`) |
@"results"!(lambda:Term`lam f. lam x. x`) |

for(@lambda:Term`${r}` <- @"results" where lambda:Term`${r}` == lambda:Term`lam f. lam x. (f, (f, (f, (f, (f, (f, x))))))`) {
  @"OUT"!(lambda:Term`${r}`)
}
